sapphire: the display's UBWC pool is on from boot, with the GPU's tiled channel order

Measured with the driver drawing the window server's framebuffer in UBWC (its framebuffer fetch, views and the 2D
engine's copies and fills now read and write the layout): the panel shows it clean, and over the same gesture (n=3,
9 s each) the queue flips 53/s linear and 65/s UBWC, the GPU busy about 91 % and 72 % of the time.

Defaults change: kern.sweet_gpu_ubwc 1 (kgsl's values, bank bit 14), kern.sweet_fb_scanout 1 and kern.sweet_fb_ubwc
1, so the pool's surfaces are made UBWC from the window server's first frame; boot-args gpu_ubwc=0, sweetfb_scanout=0
and sweetfb_ubwc=0 turn each off, as the sysctls do. kern.sweet_fb_ubwc_unpack defaults to 0x03010002: in TILE6_3 the
GPU keeps the components in WZYX order whatever the texture's format (Mesa fd6_pipe2swap: the CCU ignores the swap
when tiled), so a BGRA surface is R,G,B,A in memory and the plane reads it with the unpack of the phone's Android for
UBWC ABGR8888; with the BGRA pattern red and blue were swapped. scanoutInit() no longer refuses UBWC at boot: a frame
of the copy path is linear and planeScaled() restores the plane's linear registers for it (0403).

